  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Calibrated",
    "overview": "FlexTrack is a meet-day competition platform. Colour is a measurement, not decoration: the only hues in the app are the IWF calibrated-plate colours, and each one carries exactly one meaning. Everything else is rubber floor and chalk. A lifter glancing at the phone from a metre away on a bench should read state from hue and number alone, with the meaning also printed in words or digits so colour is never the only carrier.\n\nThe voice is a scoreboard. Big Shoulders Display sets every number and every title tall and condensed; Archivo carries all running text. Surfaces are filled rubber tones stacked by lightness, never outlined, and depth comes from fill rather than shadow. The signature objects are literal gym-floor instruments: a side-view loaded barbell with real plate diameters, three judges' lights, a yellow record band, a draining rest bar.\n\nThe world explicitly replaces the category default of a navy dashboard with one neon accent, glow, and icon-tile stat cards.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Rubber-black ground, filled rubber surfaces, chalk text and chalk primary actions.",
      "Plate hues are the only hues, each with a single fixed meaning.",
      "Scoreboard numerals (Big Shoulders Display, tabular) against plain Archivo text.",
      "No borders on surfaces, no glow, no eyebrows; hairlines only inside lists.",
      "Large one-handed targets (44px floor, 52 to 64px for in-session controls)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Calibrated Plate Rule",
        "body": "Plate hues are the only hues. A new colour may enter only as a plate or as a meaning already listed here.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Yellow Is a Record Rule",
        "body": "Yellow (#F3C316) means a personal record and nothing else: the record band, record points on charts, the \"new\" value mark. Never warnings, highlights or streaks.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Light Rule",
        "body": "Red (#D2232A) means push, a 25 kg plate, or a no-lift: a missed or skipped set and destructive actions. A good lift or a completed set is a chalk-white light.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Green Is Legs Rule",
        "body": "Green (#1E9B4B) belongs to the legs category only. Improvement is printed in chalk with a sign (+2.5 kg), never coloured green.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
